  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_a10dea6e090f4a97937d5455348af70a",
      "statement": "The object-store adapter implements two conditional-write dialects behind one surface: S3 and Azure Blob Storage use the etag sent as If-Match / If-None-Match, Google Cloud Storage uses the object generation sent as x-goog-if-generation-match; and put_cas answers Ok(None) only for a clean 412/409 rejection while every other failure is ambiguous because the write may have committed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/bucket.rs#L1-L25",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d63a1cc655e23e0612dd9d0a739a9a66c55d066ab420595e27628dd4b558dcfe:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/bucket.rs#L67-L137",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c528e144a6d911821a319e946a96a1a50fe8ca0cf72a0b8a8a3b73076c9f0958:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8a375e005e644055aac54c4eca867eb3",
      "statement": "Each cell has one ownership record at cells/<cell>/own.json naming the owner node's session and a fencing epoch; a node acquires the cell with a conditional write so the object store accepts exactly one acquisition, and every activation (takeover or local wake) advances the epoch.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/ownership_store.rs#L288-L420",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e934983f1db214fae113788119255b039e63217029245257e9aa51a03bddb451:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L1469-L1478",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eab3bb25a8fcc57f41549001cec391772fe2848220e5721114a9085265fcf3dd:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ab1df2887aaf4f79b13e40830adf103a",
      "statement": "State::output is the single choke point every egress channel passes through: nothing that reveals a cell's state leaves the process while the cell has a write it cannot prove durable; the core stores the channel but does not branch on it, so all channels share one rule.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L3-L40",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:53f4d903ee08d3c69ca81eff4abdcfbb00a425217083f1ad035ac4be0187e95b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L83-L95",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:81dd592e57b8616a138dcbe75d5ba20ecdaf80a12f1a592e72ba09fb0f1a5216:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f5150e59271b45bc8b9ec283cc223da2",
      "statement": "A write opens its own barrier and emits AwaitDurable for its committed position; durable_reached acknowledges only when the proven position covers the gated write's position, and a shorter proof fails the write rather than acknowledging one the node cannot actually restore.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L173-L196",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dd5f8f6ad3f0e796ce2fb7089162aed6e164da24cd2480086845ae3be8dbe832:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L97-L135",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2b25fbdb2d629fc4d8f2c578eb4a6eff5cde75ca410f9dac4ac96c458a4a7548:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_17b34d8f0a00494da1f18cf3d8e415da",
      "statement": "A read-only output trails the newest barrier open on its cell, because a reader can start after a write commits and before its proof lands; with nothing outstanding it releases immediately, so an ordinary read pays no durability latency.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L137-L165",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f0c327a654b1a61d8f3f1596b9dcc19f6d1ee8d1e4fef3402c65c8b202a96e35:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d162dbdbce0c4d0289a064e03c0b2902",
      "statement": "A bucket durability proof reveals nothing until ownership verification confirms the record still names this node at this epoch; a fleet proof needs no read because the ensemble arbitrated it — a takeover seals a member before restoring, so a stale owner's ack-all fails closed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L184-L212",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1803fc702a97e67cc99c0fbd8d63a2fdf4a1e094e8301b6db11f232a8fa7519c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1ef8d77f49c24400a31df0b2b7b4504d",
      "statement": "The gate also gates alarms: a firing alarm's consuming commit opens a barrier owned by GateOwner::Alarm, which settles by replay into the core (ordering the consume-side wake-entry delete after the proof) rather than by release to the shell.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L248-L274",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fde7c5399148322951d51e8b5261c1b4ac6be80582e4d13d4f32ac6d7fa218a6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L44-L57",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f14e7774d471383ac80b0b5c448c3f5e9c407ba8a891cd928083481f5ce3cfcc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b25380b548b249ddbd460f53403207b9",
      "statement": "In fleet durability mode a node streams each per-cell L0 LTX segment it captured but has not yet uploaded to a small follower ensemble over the signed peer transport; a write acknowledges when every member holds its segment on disk (write-all, ack-all) or when the ordinary bucket upload proves it first, whichever wins.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/node_log.rs#L1-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ef0da3986ab2c62be668d0180b0991e605c2dccbcfbf62d50e839970e1c07a29:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1f588d92604a448986bc7a763c2125d5",
      "statement": "The node-log record lives folded inside the node lease record (nodes/<node>.json carries a folded log object with state, epoch, ensemble, and tiered offset); the record is created before the node's first fleet-durable acknowledgement and never deleted, so a takeover that finds no record may treat the bucket as complete.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/node_log.rs#L235-L248",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:36861973e7f43c2a70efba7a7510f115fff22f15e0ec676f446bf004c1c3daee:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/ownership_store.rs#L57-L67",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9e816f65a5de2c7831ac95d2c87562f68abcd7d98f013b7d7da025896a996c29:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/log_tier.rs#L1-L19",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:09724c1212965e7c81548c2037633fcda24e9bb81a275bc06269057e7dd022c8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_788d614069574946adf26cf4ae59f105",
      "statement": "A cold activation checks the prior owner's log records before it reads the bucket: an absent record proves the session never acknowledged past the bucket, a sealed record proves recovery completed, and an open or recovering record runs recovery (fence with CAS, seal reachable followers, upload retained segments into the per-cell prefixes, mark sealed) before the cell may restore.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/node_log.rs#L676-L702",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:28ce31c9fde8724ffe319fc67afbe5d3363b6709d3dc896d0acda9ca17136620:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/types.rs#L769-L778",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bbc958651583b11b33a1be0ea032357d5b64d0945acbae8098f887be186aaf86:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_46acabb2684a4a3d953883c063648a2d",
      "statement": "A restore selects the newest epoch prefix that contains LTX data and reads the full contiguous chain from transaction zero; celld no longer writes an epoch seal object and a legacy e<epoch>.seal.json object does not limit the chain, because a node-log recovery or bundle drain can add an acknowledged tail after an earlier restore.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L185-L198",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:706453cc7954b75b23743bc2151b8252348b1152253ed70663ccbef623504817:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c790e8fb8d184544908ed6d4fc108750",
      "statement": "Each node holds a lease at nodes/<node>.json started once at process start and renewed after one third of the TTL (CELLD_TTL_MS, default 10000 ms); a renewal that lands at or after the prior lease's expiry is a fence, not a hiccup, because peers were already entitled to seize the node's cells.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L1798-L1837",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eb79818db6befc7248990de560fff4bd45f71dc120e4a2c05666bf539634406a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L1857-L1911",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b5d6b9f325cc58a71b6bc4dc3d302de0eda2480a78e1c3b250afcbaccf4599cd:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3deebb3455cf47bbb4866ee910f7ef0b",
      "statement": "node_authoritative evaluates the lease's published expiry at ask time on the monotonic clock, answering false the instant now_ms reaches expires_ms even before the fence timer fires, and the NodeLeaseFence timer uses >= to match the predicate so they cannot disagree.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L2398-L2408",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:be5be9327a55fb605b39110210fad8937b7ffbe06267fd13f3637dc403613bee:"
